{%- comment -%}
  SJ bat size guide (Off Leesh, Nov 2026). Planned with ui-ux-pro-max: design-system/sj-sports/pages/bat-size-guide.md.
  Covers every bat size, junior to adult (Harrison, 14 Nov 2026). Adult rows: Short Handle 175 to 182 cm and Long Blade /
  Long Handle about 183 cm and over, from Kookaburra's size chart (brands differ; Vik to confirm). SJ's tall bats are size LB.
  Used by templates/article.sj-size-guide.json, which is assigned to the article "What size cricket bat for my child?"
  (Online Store > Blog posts > the post > Theme template). Other blog posts keep the normal article template.
  Copy comes from the article (en dashes rewritten as "to"). Edits to the post body in Shopify admin do not change this
  page, so keep the two in step. The dead Kookaburra Kahuna Pro 9.0 link is replaced by the Kookaburra Empower Pro 9.0.
  Size finder: height in cm picks the row in the chart (between sizes it picks the smaller one, as the article says) and
  links to the bat collection filtered to that size, best sellers first.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings
  assign rows = 'Size 0|Under 120 cm|4 to 5 years|size 0|119.9|/collections/cricket-bat?sort_by=best-selling&filter.v.option.size=0|Junior;Size 1|120 to 129 cm|5 to 6 years|size 1|129|/collections/cricket-bat?sort_by=best-selling&filter.v.option.size=1|Junior;Size 2|129 to 137 cm|6 to 7 years|size 2|137|/collections/cricket-bat?sort_by=best-selling&filter.v.option.size=2|Junior;Size 3|137 to 144 cm|8 to 9 years|size 3|144|/collections/cricket-bat?sort_by=best-selling&filter.v.option.size=3|Junior;Size 4|144 to 150 cm|9 to 10 years|size 4|150|/collections/cricket-bat?sort_by=best-selling&filter.v.option.size=4|Junior;Size 5|150 to 157 cm|10 to 11 years|size 5|157|/collections/cricket-bat?sort_by=best-selling&filter.v.option.size=5|Junior;Size 6|157 to 163 cm|11 to 13 years|size 6|163|/collections/cricket-bat?sort_by=best-selling&filter.v.option.size=6|Junior;Harrow|163 to 168 cm|12 to 14 years|Harrow|168|/collections/cricket-bat?sort_by=best-selling&filter.v.option.size=H|Teens and smaller adults;Small Adult (SM / Academy)|168 to 175 cm|14 years and over|Small Adult|174.9|/collections/cricket-bat?sort_by=best-selling&filter.v.option.size=SM&filter.v.option.size=Small+Adult&filter.v.option.size=Academy|Teens and smaller adults;Short Handle (SH, full size)|175 to 182 cm|Most adults|Short Handle|182.9|/collections/cricket-bat?sort_by=best-selling&filter.v.option.size=SH|Adults;Long Blade or Long Handle (LB / LH)|About 183 cm and over|Taller adults|Long Blade|999|/collections/cricket-bat-senior-lb-lh-bats?sort_by=best-selling|Adults' | split: ';'
  assign start = s.start | default: 140
  assign heading = s.heading | default: 'Cricket bat size chart'
-%}
{%- if collection -%}
  {%- comment -%} Fetched as /collections/cricket-bat-cricket-bat-seniors?sort_by=best-selling&section_id=sj-size-guide {%- endcomment -%}
  <ul data-sjsg-cards>
    {%- assign n = 0 -%}
    {%- for p in collection.products -%}
      {%- if n >= 4 %}{% break %}{% endif -%}
      {%- if p.available == false or p.featured_media == blank %}{% continue %}{% endif -%}
      {%- assign n = n | plus: 1 -%}
      {%- render 'sj-card', product: p, rank: n, eager: false -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  </ul>
{%- else -%}
{{ 'sj-collection.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<div class="sjsg" data-sjsg>
  {%- render 'sj-home-sprite' -%}

  {%- comment -%} 1 hero with the size finder {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="sjsg-hero" aria-labelledby="sjsg-h1">
    <div class="in">
      <div class="txt">
        <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="{{ blog.url }}">{{ blog.title }}</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Bat size guide</span></nav>
        <p class="eye">Bat size guide, junior to adult</p>
        <h1 id="sjsg-h1">{{ heading }}</h1>
        <p class="lede"><b>Quick answer:</b> choose a cricket bat by height, not age. Use the chart below. If you fall between two sizes, pick the smaller, lighter bat: players learn better technique with a bat they can control. Never buy a junior a bat to "grow into".</p>
        <ul class="facts" role="list">
          <li><svg class="i"><use href="#sjh-ruler"/></svg><span>Sized by height, not age</span></li>
          <li><svg class="i"><use href="#sjh-cbat"/></svg><span>Size 0 to long blade</span></li>
          <li><svg class="i"><use href="#sjh-store"/></svg><span>Try sizes in Woolloongabba</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      {%- liquid
        assign first = ''
        for r in rows
          assign c = r | split: '|'
          assign mx = c[4] | plus: 0
          if start <= mx
            assign first = c
            break
          endif
        endfor
      -%}
      <div class="finder" data-sjsg-finder>
        <h2 class="ft">Find the right size</h2>
        <label class="fl" for="sjsg-h">Player's height in bare feet</label>
        <div class="hrow">
          <input id="sjsg-h" class="num" type="number" inputmode="numeric" min="80" max="210" step="1" value="{{ start }}" data-sjsg-num aria-describedby="sjsg-res">
          <span class="unit">cm</span>
        </div>
        <input class="rng" type="range" min="100" max="200" step="1" value="{{ start }}" aria-label="Player's height in centimetres" data-sjsg-rng>
        <div class="scale" aria-hidden="true"><span>100 cm</span><span>200 cm</span></div>
        <div class="res" id="sjsg-res" aria-live="polite">
          <span class="rl">Bat size</span>
          <b data-sjsg-size>{{ first[0] }}</b>
          <span class="rm" data-sjsg-meta>{{ first[1] }}, usually {{ first[2] | downcase }}</span>
        </div>
        <a class="btn cta" href="{{ first[5] }}" data-sjsg-shop><span>Shop {{ first[3] }} bats</span><svg class="i"><use href="#sjh-arrow"/></svg></a>
        <p class="tip"><svg class="i"><use href="#sjh-info"/></svg>Between sizes? Pick the smaller one.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <nav class="sjsg-jump" aria-label="On this page">
    <div class="in"><ul role="list">
      <li><a href="#sjsg-chart">Size chart</a></li>
      <li><a href="#sjsg-check">Check at home</a></li>
      <li><a href="#sjsg-adult">Teen and adult bats</a></li>
      <li><a href="#sjsg-willow">Kashmir or English willow</a></li>
      <li><a href="#sjsg-bats">Popular bats</a></li>
      <li><a href="#sjsg-kit">Junior kit sizes</a></li>
      <li><a href="#sjsg-faq">Questions</a></li>
    </ul></div>
  </nav>

  {%- comment -%} 2 chart {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="sjsg-sec" id="sjsg-chart" aria-labelledby="sjsg-chart-h">
    <div class="in">
      <p class="eye">Size chart</p>
      <h2 class="h2" id="sjsg-chart-h">Cricket bat size chart <span>(by height)</span></h2>
      <div class="chart-wrap">
        <table class="chart">
          <caption class="sr">Cricket bat sizes by the player's height, junior to adult, with a typical age as a guide</caption>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Bat size</th><th scope="col">Player's height</th><th scope="col">Typical age <small>(guide only)</small></th><th scope="col"><span class="sr">Shop this size</span></th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {%- assign grp = '' -%}
            {%- for r in rows -%}
              {%- assign c = r | split: '|' -%}
              {%- if c[6] != grp -%}{%- assign grp = c[6] -%}<tr class="grp"><th colspan="4" scope="colgroup">{{ grp }}</th></tr>{%- endif -%}
              <tr data-sjsg-row data-max="{{ c[4] }}" data-name="{{ c[0] | escape }}" data-meta="{{ c[1] }}, usually {{ c[2] | downcase }}" data-short="{{ c[3] }}" data-url="{{ c[5] }}"{% if c[0] == first[0] %} class="is-on"{% endif %}>
                <th scope="row"><span class="tag">Best match</span>{{ c[0] }}</th>
                <td>{{ c[1] }}</td>
                <td>{{ c[2] }}</td>
                <td class="go"><a href="{{ c[5] }}" aria-label="Shop {{ c[3] }} bats"><span>Shop</span><svg class="i"><use href="#sjh-arrow"/></svg></a></td>
              </tr>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="fine">Sizes vary slightly between brands, so treat the chart as a starting point. Long blade and long handle sizes vary the most.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} 3 check at home {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="sjsg-sec soft" id="sjsg-check" aria-labelledby="sjsg-check-h">
    <div class="in">
      <p class="eye">At home</p>
      <h2 class="h2" id="sjsg-check-h">How to check the size <span>at home</span></h2>
      <ol class="steps" role="list">
        <li><span class="no">1</span><h3>Measure height</h3><p>In bare feet, standing against a wall.</p></li>
        <li><span class="no">2</span><h3>Stand the bat beside the player</h3><p>Toe of the bat on the floor beside their foot. The top of the handle should sit just below the hip joint. If it reaches their waist or higher, the bat is too long.</p></li>
        <li><span class="no">3</span><h3>Do the one-hand test</h3><p>Hold the bat by the handle in their top hand, arm straight out in front, for a few seconds. If the bat drops or wobbles, it's too heavy.</p></li>
        <li><span class="no">4</span><h3>Take a stance</h3><p>In their batting stance the bat should rest comfortably next to their back foot, without them bending over or choking down the handle.</p></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="note">
        <h3>Between sizes? Go smaller</h3>
        <p>A bat that's too big or heavy pulls players, especially kids, into bad habits: a slow backlift, dropping the shoulder and swinging across the line. A lighter bat lets them play straight, react quickly and enjoy batting. Juniors will have a better season with the right size now than with a bigger bat they "grow into".</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} 4 teen and adult bats {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="sjsg-sec" id="sjsg-adult" aria-labelledby="sjsg-adult-h">
    <div class="in">
      <p class="eye">Teens and adults</p>
      <h2 class="h2" id="sjsg-adult-h">Teen and <span>adult bats</span></h2>
      <div class="kit">
        <div class="kc">
          <h3>Harrow and Small Adult</h3>
          <p class="how">For teens and smaller adults. Harrow suits about 163 to 168 cm, Small Adult (SM or Academy) about 168 to 175 cm.</p>
          <a class="more" href="/collections/cricket-bat-harrow-sm-bats?sort_by=best-selling">Shop Harrow and SM bats<svg class="i"><use href="#sjh-arrow"/></svg></a>
        </div>
        <div class="kc">
          <h3>Short Handle (SH)</h3>
          <p class="how">The standard full-size bat that most adults use, about 175 to 182 cm.</p>
          <a class="more" href="/collections/cricket-bat-cricket-bat-seniors?sort_by=best-selling">Shop senior bats<svg class="i"><use href="#sjh-arrow"/></svg></a>
        </div>
        <div class="kc">
          <h3>Long Blade or Long Handle</h3>
          <p class="how">A longer blade or handle for taller players, about 183 cm and over. Brands size these differently, so it's worth trying one in store.</p>
          <a class="more" href="/collections/cricket-bat-senior-lb-lh-bats?sort_by=best-selling">Shop long blade bats<svg class="i"><use href="#sjh-arrow"/></svg></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} 4 willow {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="sjsg-sec" id="sjsg-willow" aria-labelledby="sjsg-willow-h">
    <div class="in">
      <p class="eye">Which willow</p>
      <h2 class="h2" id="sjsg-willow-h">Kashmir willow or <span>English willow?</span></h2>
      <div class="willow">
        <div class="wc">
          <h3>Kashmir willow</h3>
          <ul class="pts" role="list"><li>Best for beginners</li><li>Most durable</li><li>Much cheaper</li></ul>
          <p>Kashmir willow is harder, more durable and much cheaper. It's the best choice for beginners, backyard cricket and kids who are growing fast. Most young players are perfectly served by a Kashmir bat.</p>
          <a class="more" href="/collections/cricket-bat-junior-kashmir-willow?sort_by=best-selling">Shop junior Kashmir willow bats<svg class="i"><use href="#sjh-arrow"/></svg></a>
        </div>
        <div class="wc">
          <h3>English willow</h3>
          <ul class="pts" role="list"><li>Lighter for its size</li><li>More ping</li><li>Club cricket</li></ul>
          <p>English willow is lighter for its size and gives more "ping" off the middle, so it suits keen players, juniors included, playing club cricket with a hard ball. It needs knocking in and occasional oiling before use.</p>
          <p class="prep"><svg class="i"><use href="#sjh-check"/></svg><span>We oil and knock in every English willow bat for free before it ships. <a href="/pages/free-bat-preparation-service">About free bat prep</a></span></p>
          <a class="more" href="/collections/cricket-bat-cricket-bat-juniors?sort_by=best-selling">Shop junior English willow bats<svg class="i"><use href="#sjh-arrow"/></svg></a>
          <a class="more" href="/collections/cricket-bat-cricket-bat-seniors?sort_by=best-selling">Shop senior English willow bats<svg class="i"><use href="#sjh-arrow"/></svg></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} 5 popular junior bats {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="sjsg-sec soft" id="sjsg-bats" aria-labelledby="sjsg-bats-h">
    <div class="in">
      <div class="row-head">
        <div><p class="eye">Popular at SJ Sports</p><h2 class="h2" id="sjsg-bats-h">Popular <span>junior bats</span></h2></div>
        <a class="more" href="/collections/cricket-bat-cricket-bat-juniors?sort_by=best-selling">See all junior bats<svg class="i"><use href="#sjh-arrow"/></svg></a>
      </div>
      <div class="sjcol sjsg-rail"><ul class="sjcol-grid" role="list">
        {%- if s.products != blank -%}
          {%- for p in s.products -%}{%- render 'sj-card', product: p, rank: 0, eager: false -%}{%- endfor -%}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- assign picks = 'gray-nicolls-vapour-strike-junior-kashmir-willow-cricket-bat,kookaburra-empower-pro-9-0-junior-kashmir-willow-bat-2,gray-nicolls-nova-4-0-1200-english-willow-junior-cricket-bat,gray-nicolls-cricket-set-small-junior-ambidextrous-2026' | split: ',' -%}
          {%- for h in picks -%}{%- assign p = all_products[h] -%}{%- if p != blank and p.available -%}{%- render 'sj-card', product: p, rank: 0, eager: false -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      </ul></div>
      <div class="row-head adult" data-sjsg-adult data-url="/collections/cricket-bat-cricket-bat-seniors?sort_by=best-selling&section_id=sj-size-guide">
        <div><h2 class="h2">Best-selling <span>adult bats</span></h2></div>
        <a class="more" href="/collections/cricket-bat-cricket-bat-seniors?sort_by=best-selling">See all senior bats<svg class="i"><use href="#sjh-arrow"/></svg></a>
      </div>
      <div class="sjcol sjsg-rail" data-sjsg-adult-grid><ul class="sjcol-grid" role="list" aria-busy="true">
        {%- for i in (1..4) -%}<li class="sjsg-skel" aria-hidden="true"><span class="im"></span><span class="l"></span><span class="l s"></span></li>{%- endfor -%}
      </ul></div>
      <div class="bigger">
        <span>More sizes:</span>
        <a href="/collections/cricket-bat-harrow-sm-bats?sort_by=best-selling">Harrow bats</a>
        <a href="/collections/small-adult-bats">Small Adult bats</a>
        <a href="/collections/cricket-bat-senior-lb-lh-bats?sort_by=best-selling">Long blade bats</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} 6 rest of the kit {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="sjsg-sec" id="sjsg-kit" aria-labelledby="sjsg-kit-h">
    <div class="in">
      <p class="eye">Junior kit sizes</p>
      <h2 class="h2" id="sjsg-kit-h">Sizing the rest of <span>a junior's kit</span></h2>
      <div class="kit">
        <div class="kc">
          <h3>Batting gloves</h3>
          <p class="how"><b>How to measure:</b> wrist crease to tip of middle finger.</p>
          <dl><div><dt>Small Junior</dt><dd>about 16.5 cm</dd></div><div><dt>Junior</dt><dd>about 17.5 cm</dd></div><div><dt>Youth</dt><dd>about 19 cm</dd></div></dl>
          <a class="more" href="/collections/cricket-batting-gloves-junior-gloves">Shop junior gloves<svg class="i"><use href="#sjh-arrow"/></svg></a>
        </div>
        <div class="kc">
          <h3>Helmet</h3>
          <p class="how"><b>How to measure:</b> head circumference with a soft tape, just above the eyebrows.</p>
          <dl><div><dt>Junior Small</dt><dd>51 to 52 cm</dd></div><div><dt>Junior</dt><dd>53 to 54 cm</dd></div><div><dt>Youth</dt><dd>54 to 56 cm</dd></div></dl>
          <a class="more" href="/collections/cricket-helmets-junior-helmets">Shop junior helmets<svg class="i"><use href="#sjh-arrow"/></svg></a>
        </div>
        <div class="kc">
          <h3>Batting pads</h3>
          <p class="how"><b>How to measure:</b> centre of kneecap to top of foot.</p>
          <dl><div><dt>Small Junior</dt><dd>30 to 32 cm</dd></div><div><dt>Junior</dt><dd>32 to 34 cm</dd></div><div><dt>Youth</dt><dd>34 to 37 cm</dd></div></dl>
          <a class="more" href="/collections/cricket-batting-pads-junior-pads">Shop junior pads<svg class="i"><use href="#sjh-arrow"/></svg></a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="kits"><b>Starting from scratch?</b> A cricket kit has the bat, gloves, pads and more in one box. <a href="/collections/cricket-kits">Shop cricket kits</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} 7 questions {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="sjsg-sec soft" id="sjsg-faq" aria-labelledby="sjsg-faq-h">
    <div class="in">
      <p class="eye">Questions</p>
      <h2 class="h2" id="sjsg-faq-h">Frequently asked <span>questions</span></h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <details><summary>What size cricket bat does an 8-year-old need?<svg class="i"><use href="#sjh-chev"/></svg></summary><p>Most 8-year-olds use a size 3 (for a height of about 137 to 144 cm). A smaller 8-year-old may need a size 2. Always check their height against the chart.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What size cricket bat for a 10-year-old?<svg class="i"><use href="#sjh-chev"/></svg></summary><p>Usually a size 4 or size 5, depending on height: size 4 for 144 to 150 cm, size 5 for 150 to 157 cm.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What size cricket bat for a 12-year-old?<svg class="i"><use href="#sjh-chev"/></svg></summary><p>Usually a size 6 (157 to 163 cm). Taller 12-year-olds may be ready for a Harrow (163 to 168 cm).</p></details>
        <details><summary>When should my child move to a Harrow or full-size bat?<svg class="i"><use href="#sjh-chev"/></svg></summary><p>Move to a Harrow at about 163 cm, a Small Adult at about 168 cm, and a full-size Short Handle at about 175 cm.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What size cricket bat does an adult need?<svg class="i"><use href="#sjh-chev"/></svg></summary><p>Most adults use a Short Handle (SH), about 175 to 182 cm. Taller players, about 183 cm and over, may suit a long blade or long handle. Teens and smaller adults often use a Harrow or Small Adult.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Should I buy a bigger bat so they can grow into it?<svg class="i"><use href="#sjh-chev"/></svg></summary><p>No. An oversized bat is heavier and longer, which makes good technique harder and can put kids off batting. Buy the size that fits now.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can left-handed kids use any bat?<svg class="i"><use href="#sjh-chev"/></svg></summary><p>Yes, bats themselves aren't left- or right-handed. Starter kits like the Gray-Nicolls Junior Cricket Set are ambidextrous, so the gloves and pads suit both.</p></details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} 8 close {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="sjsg-end" aria-labelledby="sjsg-end-h">
    <div class="in">
      <div><h2 id="sjsg-end-h">Still not sure? <span>Try sizes in store</span></h2><p>Come in to SJ Sports, 60 Deshon Street, Woolloongabba (Brisbane), and we'll help you or your young cricketer find the right bat and gear.</p></div>
      <div class="ctas">
        <a class="btn sun" href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=SJ+Sports+60+Deshon+St+Woolloongabba" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="i"><use href="#sjh-pin"/></svg>Get directions</a>
        <a class="btn ghost" href="tel:0423240478"><svg class="i"><use href="#sjh-phone"/></svg>Call 0423 240 478</a>
      </div>
